==English==

===Etymology===
{{wikipedia}}
From the Latin [[circa]], meaning "around" and [[dies]], "day", meaning literally, "around a day".

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-circadian_rhythm.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
# The "[[internal]] [[body clock]]" that regulates the (roughly) 24-hour cycle of [[biological]] processes in animals and plants.

